  `captures()`; TS grammar names class names type_identifier (a wrong
  node type fails the WHOLE query — caught by the cross-language test).

WHAT CHANGED
---------------------------------------------------------------------
- crates/retrieval/src/lexical.rs (new): Tantivy in-RAM index per task;
  one doc per indexed file; incremental replace by exact path term
  (delete_term + add), committed once per delta batch; unparsable query
  syntax -> empty, never a panic; deterministic tie-break by path.
- crates/retrieval/src/symbols.rs (new): tree-sitter definitions
  (function/method/class/struct/enum/trait/module/interface/type_alias)
  for Rust, TypeScript, TSX, JavaScript, Python + per-file identifier
  occurrence spans. references(name) is a QUERY-TIME VIEW over the
  current global definition set minus definition sites — a definition
  added later resolves occurrences indexed before it existed with no
  reparse, so incremental updates and cold builds answer identically
  (per-file purity).
- crates/retrieval/src/task_index.rs: TaskIndex gains `lexical` +
  `symbols`, both maintained by build_at/apply_delta; context_query()
  fuses BM25 (normalized, weight 1.0) + exact symbol definitions
  (weight 1.2) + case-insensitive path match (weight 0.6), merged per
  path with provenance and deterministic ordering; symbol_definitions /
  symbol_references accessors. Paths + provenance only — content bytes
  always hydrate from the live file (docs/18 freshness rule).
- crates/core-runtime/scheduler.rs: `context.query` and `search.symbol`
  tools registered (ReadOnly, granted in worktree_grants); both drain
  the change journal BEFORE answering (refresh reason context_query /
  symbol_query); a missing task index degrades to an explicit empty
  result, never an error.

